      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s kinda odd to represent regular label lists as globs, isn\u0027t it? \n\nMy line of thinking is that this will eventually morph into the description of a regular label list attribute and I don\u0027t think a single Glob instance is the right way to represent that.\n\nI think you can go two ways:\n\n1. Make bazelFilegroupAttributes already represent the Bazel data structure, which is something like\n\nLabelListAttr ::\u003d Element*\nElement ::\u003d LabelList | Glob\nLabelList :\u003d Label*\nGlob \u003d \u003cincludes, excludes, etc.\u003e",
